{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"amphibolic-saccharine-goral","creation_channel":"cli","description":"`_engine_support/reads.py:133-137` and `:151-157` print to stderr and call `sys.exit(1)` when the\nrepo root is not a git worktree. That function is reached from the library gate surface\n(`_lib_gates.py:42,68,83,109,118,163,210`) and thence from MCP (`_mcp_reads.py:212,218,224`).\n\nEmpirically proven during verification: a real in-memory FastMCP client was driven against a tool\nthat exits this way. FastMCP catches `Exception` (`mcp/server/fastmcp/tools/base.py:116`) and\n`SystemExit` is a `BaseException`, so the whole `anyio.run` dies — the MCP server PROCESS\nterminates rather than returning a tool error.\n\nTrigger is narrow (REBAR_ROOT unset with a non-repo cwd, or the repo vanishing mid-session), but a\nleaf helper unilaterally deciding process lifetime for every embedding surface is the defect. The\nlibrary contract is to raise `RebarError`.\n\nBoth remediation proposers converged: convert to a domain exception and map it to exit 1 at the CLI\nboundary ONLY, so the CLI's observable behaviour is unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `tracker_dir()` raises a rebar error instead of calling `sys.exit`\n- [ ] The CLI maps that error to exit 1 with the same message as today\n- [ ] A test asserts an MCP tool returns an error payload (not a dead server) with REBAR_ROOT unset in a non-repo cwd\n- [ ] No `sys.exit` remains reachable from `_lib_*` or `_mcp_*`","id":"176d-6bb4-df56-49cd","parent_id":"b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181","priority":2,"tags":["janitor"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Remove sys.exit from the shared read core"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786046997702443001,"uuid":"74c6fb6f-bc8d-4cb6-97e0-90211b3d6242"}